Backport-style fix for riscv64 (SpacemiT K1): bpf_timer_init() failed
unconditionally with -ENOMEM.

kmalloc_nolock() (mm/slub.c) returns NULL on every architecture whose
caches are not flagged __CMPXCHG_DOUBLE, i.e. those without a 128-bit
compare-and-swap: x86 needs CPUID CX16, arm64/s390 always provide it,
but riscv64 requires the Zacas extension (AMOCAS.Q) at runtime, which
SpacemiT K1 (C920 cores) does not implement, and riscv does not select
CONFIG_HAVE_CMPXCHG_DOUBLE in this tree either way.

bpf_timer_init() is the only user of bpf_map_kmalloc_nolock() in this
tree (kernel/bpf/helpers.c __bpf_async_init), so every bpf_timer_init()
-- including the one in landscape's nat4_insert_ct() -- returned -ENOMEM
and dropped all NATed flows.  x86/arm64 are unaffected.

Fix follows the same direction as the upstream discussion
"[PATCH bpf v3] bpf: do not use kmalloc_nolock when !HAVE_CMPXCHG_DOUBLE"
(Levi Zim, 2026-03): keep kmalloc_nolock() where it is supported or
required for correctness (PREEMPT_RT), and use a plain GFP_NOWAIT
allocation otherwise.  GFP_NOWAIT never sleeps, so it is valid under the
irqsave async->lock held in __bpf_async_init() and works on every
architecture.  The free side (kfree_nolock) works on all architectures
(it falls back to slab_lock) and needs no change.
--- a/kernel/bpf/helpers.c
+++ b/kernel/bpf/helpers.c
@@ -1295,7 +1295,18 @@
 		goto out;
 	}
 
-	cb = bpf_map_kmalloc_nolock(map, size, 0, map->numa_node);
+	/*
+	 * kmalloc_nolock() always returns NULL on architectures without
+	 * CONFIG_HAVE_CMPXCHG_DOUBLE (e.g. riscv64 without Zacas), making
+	 * bpf_timer_init() fail with -ENOMEM unconditionally.  GFP_NOWAIT
+	 * never sleeps and is valid under the irqsave async->lock held
+	 * above; PREEMPT_RT keeps kmalloc_nolock() for correctness.
+	 */
+	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_HAVE_CMPXCHG_DOUBLE) && !IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT))
+		cb = bpf_map_kmalloc_node(map, size, GFP_NOWAIT | __GFP_NOWARN | __GFP_NOMEMALLOC,
+					  map->numa_node);
+	else
+		cb = bpf_map_kmalloc_nolock(map, size, 0, map->numa_node);
 	if (!cb) {
 		ret = -ENOMEM;
 		goto out;
